# What the Fly build does *not* upload to the builder.
#
# Nothing here can put a hole in the image on its own, because
# `Dockerfile.fly` copies named paths and never `COPY . .`; the list exists so the builder
# is handed the deployment and not the workshop around it. `test/docker-context.test.js`
# reads the two files against each other and fails if they disagree either way — a path
# copied but excluded, or a path uploaded that nothing copies.
.git
.github
.claude
.claude-plugin
.worktrees
# Two agent harnesses keep their worktrees here, and neither belongs in a build
# context: `.worktrees` above is this project's own, these are the other two.
.rovodev
# The maintainers' workflow notes. Nothing in the image reads them, and the new
# context check below is what noticed they were being uploaded.
.maintainers
.output
node_modules
docs
# ...except the docs that are pages: they are served by the app, not read in the
# repository. See Dockerfile.fly, which copies them.
!docs/*.html
# ...the built documentation site, which is served at /docs. Only the site: the markdown
# it was generated from stays out, since nothing reads it at runtime.
#
# Both the directory and its contents are re-included, and the single-level forms are
# spelled out beside the `**` ones deliberately. `docs` above excludes the whole tree, and
# a parent directory that stays excluded is a directory the build never walks into — so
# the exceptions have to name each level they descend through. The previous version of
# this file enumerated `docs/images`, `docs/images/objects` and `docs/images/objects/*` for
# exactly that reason, and this is that lesson kept rather than tidied away: a wrong guess
# here is a deployed office whose documentation is entirely 404, and nothing local says so.
!docs/site
!docs/site/*
!docs/site/**
# ...and all the doc imagery, which the served prose and the editor's add menu both need.
!docs/images
!docs/images/*
!docs/images/**
# ...and the downloadable examples the docs link at.
!docs/examples
!docs/examples/*
!docs/examples/**
# The Codex half of the plugin distribution. `plugins/claude` is served and ships; this
# is a Git repository's worth of files waiting for a Git repository, it is gitignored, and
# nothing serves a clone.
plugins/codex
inspo
# The tools rather than the product: the adapters and hooks a laptop runs to feed the
# office, and the suite that checks the room. Nothing in the image runs any of them.
bin
hooks
test
# Development configuration, and the artifacts built with it. The lockfile is in here
# because this image deliberately runs no `npm install` — see the header of
# `Dockerfile.fly` — so nothing in the build or the container ever resolves it, `.npmrc`
# included. `dist` is the packed OpenClaw install, which is gitignored and served by
# nobody.
package-lock.json
.npmrc
eslint.config.js
eleventy.config.mjs
.eleventyignore
.exportignore
.gitignore
dist
# The plugin *sources*. `plugins/` above is the published pair of artifacts and ships
# because the site serves them by URL; these are the trees the packers build them from,
# and a server runs neither.
.codex-plugin
openclaw-plugin
# Records that are read in the repository: the machine-readable provenance evidence
# regenerated by `bin/gen-third-party.mjs`, the research logs, one personal layout file
# and an ownership marker. Some of these are not in the public export either, which is
# why a clone may not have them — see `.exportignore`.
third-party
autoresearch
mcb
.atlassian
# Prose about the project rather than the product, none of it served: the working
# agreements, the policies, the asset and licence records.
#
# `THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt` is the one attribution file the image does carry, and
# `Dockerfile.fly` copies it deliberately, because the browser downloads the three.js it
# covers and that licence has to travel with the copy. `LICENSE` and `NOTICE` cover this
# repository's own code and artwork, which a deployment does not hand out — if that ever
# stops being true they belong in a `COPY` in both recipes, not in a line removed here.
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md
README.md
CONTRIBUTING.md
CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md
SECURITY.md
ASSETS.md
LICENSE
NOTICE
program.md
tro-2-automation-rules.md
# The Finder's litter.
.DS_Store
# The deploy recipes, including this file: the builder is handed the Dockerfile by the
# client and has read the ignore list before the upload starts, and the other target's
# recipes are no business of this one's.
Dockerfile.fly
.dockerignore
fly.toml
bitbucket-pipelines.yml
